2. The wait no longer blocks the loop (finding 2). start() no longer waits: while lingerDone is set it records the start in `held` and returns (supervisor.go:682-694). The loop runs it from a new select case on lingerDone (:974-984). Branches and the state each runs in:
 - start() gate: runs with cmd == nil. A kept job (lingerDone) exists only after the exit branch handed a failed run's job to closeAfterReporter, which is the branch that cleared cmd. While lingerDone is set no start reaches the spawn, so no process runs. Known from the code: the only spawn is below this gate.
 - case <-lingerDone: cmd == nil (same invariant). held != nil only while desired, because ctrlStop drops it. start() still checks ctx first, so nothing starts during a shutdown.
 - ctrlStop (:835-838): desired = false, backoff and held dropped, stop() is a no-op since cmd == nil. The kept job is left to closeAfterReporter: it closes when the reporter finishes, the grace ends or the launcher shuts down. So a stop during the wait cancels the pending restart, as a stop during the restart delay did, and the reporter can outlive the stop by up to the grace. Pinned by TestStopDuringTheWaitForTheCrashReporterCancelsTheStart (no second start, job closed once). Mutation: without clearing held the test goes red.
 - ctrlStart/ctrlRestart during the wait: cmd == nil, so restart's stop() is a no-op and start(pre) puts it in held, replacing the earlier one. It runs once on lingerDone. replacesRestart (:813-822) also counts a held Automatic/ReplacesRestart start as the policy's pending start, so the start keeps Saved/Crashes (followsCrash). Pinned by TestStartDuringTheWaitForTheCrashReporterIsHeld (start and restart: answered at once, not running, waiting set, no error; one start after the release, Start{ReplacesRestart:true}, never a third).
 - backoff case: the timer's start(Automatic) is held, so the start comes at max(restart delay, reporter done). TestRestartWaitsForTheCrashReporterOfTheLastRun still covers this.
 - ctx.Done case: unchanged. It waits for lingerDone, which closeAfterReporter closes at once on ctx.
 Status during the wait: the loop answers. It reports running false, desired true, lastExit, and a new field ServiceStatus.Waiting = "crash-reporter" (supervisor.go:156-160) while a start is held. No busy or unresponsive. TestStatusDuringTheWaitForTheCrashReporter replaces TestStatusNamesTheWaitForTheCrashReporterAsPreStart, which pinned the blocking. Busy/preStarting docs are back to PreStart only.
 Launcher: a held start answers with not running, so ue_start/ue_restart (serviceAction, tools.go:238-240) and the console's start/r (lifecycle.go:492-493) would have called it "did not start: " with an empty error. They now say the start is held and comes on its own (startHeld, tools.go:253-258), and it is no tool error. Pinned by TestServiceActionReportsAHeldStartAsNoError (tools_test.go). The console branch has no test of its own: a held state needs the supervisor's unexported probe. The status, ue_start and ue_restart tool descriptions name "waiting": "crash-reporter" (tools.go:24, 42, 54).

